! Constructions from the PDF (Chicago 5A, new construction, 90.1-2004): wall U = 0.151 Btu/h-ft2-F (Table 21, mass wall: the xlsx names a concrete block wall), roof U = 0.063 (Table 19, insulation entirely above deck). The layer resistance is 1/U minus the surface films.
  Material:NoMass,
    ExteriorWallLayer,            !- Name  Source: NREL PDF Table 21, p.37: mass wall U = 0.151 Btu/h-ft2-F; R = 1/U - films (0.1496 m2-K/W: interior 0.1197 + exterior 0.0299, 90.1-2004) = 1.0167 m2-K/W.
    MediumRough,                  !- Roughness
    1.0167;                       !- Thermal Resistance {m2-K/W}

  Construction,
    ExteriorWall,                 !- Name
    ExteriorWallLayer;            !- Outside Layer

  Material:NoMass,
    RoofLayer,                    !- Name  Source: NREL PDF Table 19, p.36: roof U = 0.063 Btu/h-ft2-F; R = 1/U - films (0.1373 m2-K/W: interior 0.1074 + exterior 0.0299, 90.1-2004) = 2.6581 m2-K/W.
    MediumRough,                  !- Roughness
    2.6581;                       !- Thermal Resistance {m2-K/W}

  Construction,
    Roof,                         !- Name
    RoofLayer;                    !- Outside Layer

  Material:NoMass,
    GenericLayer,                 !- Name  Not in the documents: EnergyPlus needs a construction for the interior walls; the resistance 0.2 m2-K/W is assumed.
    MediumRough,                  !- Roughness
    0.2;                          !- Thermal Resistance {m2-K/W}, chosen as a round value close to the prototype interior wall construction (0.159 m2-K/W); no thermal mass

  Construction,
    GenericSurface,               !- Name
    GenericLayer;                 !- Outside Layer

  WindowMaterial:SimpleGlazingSystem,
    Glazing,                      !- Name
    3.2366,                       !- U-Factor {W/m2-K}  Source: NREL PDF Table 24, p.38: window overall U = 0.57 Btu/h-ft2-F = 3.2366 W/m2-K.
    0.39;                         !- Solar Heat Gain Coefficient  Source: NREL PDF Table 25, p.39: SHGC = 0.39.

  Construction,
    Window,                       !- Name
    Glazing;                      !- Outside Layer

! Slab on grade: F-factor method; the PDF (Table 22, p.37) gives no insulation required (NR); F = 1.26363 W/m-K is the 90.1-2004 value of an uninsulated slab. Area and perimeter are computed from the polygons.
  Construction:FfactorGroundFloor,
    Back_Space_Floor_Ffactor,     !- Name
    1.26363,                      !- F-Factor {W/m-K}
    379.8899999999999,            !- Area {m2}  Derived from: the area of the floor polygon of the surface Back_Space_Floor (379.89 m2 = 4089.102 ft2 from the vertex coordinates).
    68.27000000000001;            !- PerimeterExposed {m}  Derived from: the sum of the bottom edges of the 3 exterior walls that stand on the floor of the zone (Back_Space_Wall_East, Back_Space_Wall_North, Back_Space_Wall_West): 7 + 54.27 + 7 = 68.27 m.

  Construction:FfactorGroundFloor,
    Core_Retail_Floor_Ffactor,    !- Name
    1.26363,                      !- F-Factor {W/m-K}
    1600.4829,                    !- Area {m2}  Derived from: the area of the floor polygon of the surface Core_Retail_Floor (1600.4829 m2 = 17227.455 ft2 from the vertex coordinates).
    58.53999999999999;            !- PerimeterExposed {m}  Derived from: the sum of the bottom edges of the 2 exterior walls that stand on the floor of the zone (Core_Retail_Wall_West_2, Core_Retail_Wall_East_2): 29.27 + 29.27 = 58.54 m.

  Construction:FfactorGroundFloor,
    Point_Of_Sale_Floor_Ffactor,  !- Name
    1.26363,                      !- F-Factor {W/m-K}
    150.81,                       !- Area {m2}  Derived from: the area of the floor polygon of the surface Point_Of_Sale_Floor (150.81 m2 = 1623.305 ft2 from the vertex coordinates).
    31.135;                       !- PerimeterExposed {m}  Derived from: the sum of the bottom edges of the 2 exterior walls that stand on the floor of the zone (Point_Of_Sale_Wall_South, Point_Of_Sale_Wall_West): 25.135 + 6 = 31.135 m.

  Construction:FfactorGroundFloor,
    Front_Retail_Floor_Ffactor,   !- Name
    1.26363,                      !- F-Factor {W/m-K}
    150.81,                       !- Area {m2}  Derived from: the area of the floor polygon of the surface Front_Retail_Floor (150.81 m2 = 1623.305 ft2 from the vertex coordinates).
    31.135;                       !- PerimeterExposed {m}  Derived from: the sum of the bottom edges of the 2 exterior walls that stand on the floor of the zone (Front_Retail_Walll_East, Front_Retail_Wall_South): 6 + 25.135 = 31.135 m.

  Construction:FfactorGroundFloor,
    Front_Entry_Floor_Ffactor,    !- Name
    1.26363,                      !- F-Factor {W/m-K}
    12.0,                         !- Area {m2}  Derived from: the area of the floor polygon of the surface Front_Entry_Floor (12 m2 = 129.167 ft2 from the vertex coordinates).
    4.0;                          !- PerimeterExposed {m}  Derived from: the sum of the bottom edges of the 1 exterior wall that stand on the floor of the zone (Front_Entry_Wall_South): 4 = 4 m.

! Loads (xlsx raw_data): occupancy density m2/person (column M), lighting power density W/m2 (L), plug and process W/m2 (N), gas power W (O). The schedule of each zone is the one of its space type in the xlsx sheet Schedule Summary; where the xlsx gives no schedule for a load, the schedule AlwaysOn (the prototype schedule is constant 1) or AlwaysOff is written, because EnergyPlus needs one.
  People,
    Back_Space_People,            !- Name
    Back_Space,                   !- Zone or ZoneList or Space or SpaceList Name
    BLDG_OCC_SCH,                 !- Number of People Schedule Name  Source: xlsx Schedule Summary 'Occupants', rows 80/81/82 (Mon - Fri/Sat/Sun).
    Area/Person,                  !- Number of People Calculation Method
    ,                             !- Number of People
    ,                             !- People per Floor Area
    46.45,                        !- Floor Area per Person {m2/person}  Source: xlsx raw_data!M415 Design Occupancy Density = 46.45 m2/person.
    ,                             !- Fraction Radiant
    ,                             !- Sensible Heat Fraction
    ACTIVITY_SCH;                 !- Activity Level Schedule Name

  Lights,
    Back_Space_Lights,            !- Name
    Back_Space,                   !- Zone or ZoneList or Space or SpaceList Name
    ltg_sch_back,                 !- Schedule Name  Source: xlsx Schedule Summary 'Lighting', rows 83/84/85 (Mon - Fri/Sat/Sun).
    Watts/Area,                   !- Design Level Calculation Method
    ,                             !- Lighting Level
    9.0271;                       !- Watts per Floor Area {W/m2}  Source: xlsx raw_data!L415 Lighting Power Density = 9.0271 W/m2.

  ElectricEquipment,
    Back_Space_Equipment,         !- Name
    Back_Space,                   !- Zone or ZoneList or Space or SpaceList Name
    BLDG_EQUIP_SCH,               !- Schedule Name  Source: xlsx Schedule Summary 'Electric Equipment', rows 86/87/88 (Mon - Fri/Sat/Sun).
    Watts/Area,                   !- Design Level Calculation Method
    ,                             !- Design Level
    8.07;                         !- Watts per Floor Area {W/m2}  Source: xlsx raw_data!N415 Plug and Process = 8.07 W/m2.

  People,
    Core_Retail_People,           !- Name
